    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "The most important operational recommendation in the book is also the most counter-cultural: refactor continuously, not periodically. Dedicated \"refactoring sprints\" or \"cleanup weeks\" are symptoms of a process that has allowed debt to accumulate to the point where it needs a special event to address it. Fowler's prescription is different: refactor when you add a feature (to make room for the feature), refactor when you fix a bug (to understand the code well enough to fix it safely), and refactor during code review (to give precise feedback)."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
